{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01300",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 5.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.75,
      "end_seconds": 10.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.25,
      "end_seconds": 27.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.44,
      "text": "It's red, cracked skin on my hands. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.39,
      "end_seconds": 34.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.26,
      "end_seconds": 48.66,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "Oh, you know, I'd say two weeks. Actually, no, closer to four weeks. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.13,
      "end_seconds": 63.27,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "Understood. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.92,
      "end_seconds": 75.39,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "I'd call it severe. Yes, washing hands and gloves. That makes it worse. I've also had blisters between my fingers. Oh, and itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 79.52,
      "end_seconds": 92.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.5,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 99 percent, respiratory rate 14, temperature is 37.0 degrees, pulse is 75 beats a minute, blood pressure 111 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.04,
      "end_seconds": 94.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.07,
      "end_seconds": 99.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.84,
      "end_seconds": 103.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.28,
      "end_seconds": 121.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "The skin on both hands is red, dry and cracked in the finger creases, with no weeping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.44,
      "end_seconds": 127.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.41,
      "end_seconds": 147.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "Have you had any oozing, nail changes, joint pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.95,
      "end_seconds": 154.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.6,
      "end_seconds": 159.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.3,
      "end_seconds": 163.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.59,
      "end_seconds": 167.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.08,
      "end_seconds": 180.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "Eczema, for two years. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I have diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.02,
      "end_seconds": 189.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Right, so eczema is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.48,
      "end_seconds": 200.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I live with my elderly mother. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.28,
      "end_seconds": 205.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Right, anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.38,
      "end_seconds": 210.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Just my septum straightened, in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.68,
      "end_seconds": 214.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.52,
      "end_seconds": 220.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I'm on moisturiser, several times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.99,
      "end_seconds": 223.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Okay, when did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.35,
      "end_seconds": 226.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "For two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.25,
      "end_seconds": 239.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "So, have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.85,
      "end_seconds": 245.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Erythromycin. I come out in... well, bad stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.76,
      "end_seconds": 253.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, my working impression is irritant hand dermatitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.43,
      "end_seconds": 259.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.63,
      "end_seconds": 269.63,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like irritant hand dermatitis, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.71,
      "end_seconds": 313.41,
      "duration_seconds": 25.7,
      "text": "We should do a patch test for dermatitis. What I'm giving you is hydrocortisone 1 percent cream, 1 percent, twice a day, for one week. That's for hand dermatitis. Use gloves for washing up and moisturise straight after you dry your hands. We'll catch up in three weeks. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.83,
      "end_seconds": 321.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Mm, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}